on-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the api-stability.md change beyond a bare cross-reference: update the 'Config keys' row (and the removal-window paragraph) so it no longer asserts these renamed aliases are kept with a one-minor-release removal window, and no longer cites REBAR_SYNC_PULL←REBAR_NO_SYNC as a live retained alias, pointing to ADR 0115 for the operator-approved clean-removal policy.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.38,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["docs/api-stability.md:27 — 'renamed keys keep a **deprecated alias** ... an alias survives **at least one minor release** ... (e.g. `REBAR_SYNC_PULL` ← deprecated alias `REBAR_NO_SYNC`)'","docs/api-stability.md:30-33 — 'The **removal-window rule** applies to every \"deprecate-then-remove\" row above (CLI options, config keys, MCP tools)'","Plan Scope: 'docs/api-stability.md for the minimal cross-reference from config stability policy'","AC: 'contains a minimal cross-reference to ADR 0115 and still documents the separate strong contracts' — silent on correcting the config-keys row"],"finding":"The plan updates docs/api-stability.md only with a 'minimal cross-reference to ADR 0115' but does not require correcting the existing 'Config keys' row, which currently asserts the opposite policy (renamed keys keep a 'deprecated alias' that 'survives at least one minor release', and names 'REBAR_SYNC_PULL <- deprecated alias REBAR_NO_SYNC' as a live example). A cross-reference added beside a contradicting row leaves the doc internally inconsistent about whether these aliases are retained.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff92a9d65b04d8f61","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (docs/api-stability.md item) and Acceptance Criteria line 6","norm_id":"n0630b107dd26dd1d","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator reads api-stability.md after this ADR lands and sees both the ADR-0115 cross-reference (clean removal, no expected clients) AND the still-present claim that REBAR_NO_SYNC is a kept deprecated alias with a one-minor-release removal window."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the hardcoded 'ADR 0115' with the generator-assigned number: state the assigned number once after allocation and make the api-stability.md cross-reference and the grep verify command target that same assigned number.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["COH","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["AC line 1: 'uses the generator-assigned ADR number'","AC line 6: 'contains a minimal cross-reference to ADR 0115'","Testing: 'verify with grep that docs/api-stability.md references ADR 0115'","Approach: 'Allocate the next ADR number through docs/adr/.numbers'"],"finding":"The plan hardcodes 'ADR 0115' in Testing and Acceptance Criteria while simultaneously requiring the number be allocated by the generator through docs/adr/.numbers and calling it 'the generator-assigned ADR number'. If the generator assigns a number other than 0115, the grep proving command and AC 6 would reference the wrong number.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9c736811bbdf9fd5","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section and Acceptance Criteria lines 1 and 6","norm_id":"n8fc71595775c2424","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The .numbers allocator assigns a number != 0115; the grep proving command searches for 0115 and either fails or the doc references a wrong/nonexistent ADR."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"After allocating via docs/adr/.numbers, replace all 'ADR 0115' occurrences with the actually-assigned number, and phrase the grep as targeting the assigned number (e.g., grep -E 'ADR[[:space:]]*0*NNNN' the assigned value) rather than a pre-assumed 0115.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"non